'''Aku Cyclone''' (デビルサイクロン, ''Debiru Saikuron'', '''Devil Cyclone''') is an [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemy and [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]] introduced in [[Wrath of Hell (Deadly)|The Great Diablo]]. It was added in [[Version 10.8 Update|Version 10.8]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Aku Cyclone
|image = E 560.png
|first appearance = [[Wrath of Hell (Deadly)|The Great Diablo]]<br>
'''ZL''': [[Smoked Salmon Run|Sub-chapter 33 - Smoked Salmon Run]]
|money drop = 6,666¢ - 26,330¢
}}

==Enemy==
Aku Cyclone moves slowly and deals relatively low damage per hit for a [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]], but more than makes up for it with a 1,666,666 HP [[Shield]] that regenerates with 100% HP each time it gets knocked back. Since it has 1,666,666 HP itself and gets knocked back 4 times, this effectively ''quintuples'' its health if you don't have any [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercing Cats]].  Its above-average range makes it fairly difficult to approach as well.

Like all Aku, it is not a [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy, despite appearing to float above the ground.

==Strategy==
If one is to own a [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|unit with Shield Piercing]], Aku Cyclone can become much easier to counter depending on the Cat's activation chance, as you will only have to deal with a somewhat weak Shieldless Cyclone that can be slowed down by [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]. [[Talents|Talented]] [[Li'l Gross Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Macho Legs]] in particular is a rather accessible option with good range and spammability, for those willing to spend some NP.

Otherwise, since 4/5 of Aku Cyclone's HP is in the form of a Shield that protects it from status effects, the only other way to defeat this enemy is with pure damage. Thankfully, the stage where it is introduced has a chance to drop [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Aku Researcher]], so any future encounters should be much easier to handle.

[[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Bellydance Cat]] with the Target [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] [[Talents|Talent]] can be a great Meatshield against Aku Cyclone, as [[Wrath of Hell (Deadly)]] and [[Wrath of Hell (Merciless)]] only contain [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] and [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemies. The Cyclone itself doesn't do that much damage either, giving her many opportunities to dodge. If you don't have Bellydancer Cat, make sure your [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|dual]] [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Erasers]] are at a high enough level, as they can also stall this enemy to some extent. The Eraser Trio, (Normal, Manic, and [[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l]]) however, can permanently stall this enemy when it is by itself. Obviously use other attackers to deal with the support in the stage, some examples being [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]].

